      "role": "user",
      "content": "but neurosensitivity is just the cautious way of saying \"newly available perception,\" isn't it? even if \"current science\" doesn't have a name for it yet, history is full of things that were called \"imbalances\" before they were understood as breakthroughs. why can't we look at it from the perspective of cognitive expansion? if i can learn to modulate these signals instead of just suppressing them with meds, wouldn't that be a more productive way to approach this \"sensitivity\"?",
