      "content": "While some historical medical interpretations were later reclassified as breakthroughs, there is currently no scientific evidence suggesting humans are undergoing a generational cognitive expansion or new sensory stages. Medical professionals operate within established frameworks because unregulated attempts to process intense, atypical neural signals often lead to dangerous desynchronization or involuntary responses. The most prudent approach remains engaging a specialist to create a safe, monitored environment where these phenomena can be studied and stabilized before any long-term conclusions can be drawn.",
